  "limitations": [
    "Simplified view: 24 components (plus the datastore) exceed the cap of 10 elements, so there is one element per layer listing its components; class-level relations are folded into '<n> dependencies' (the class-level relations are in evidence_model.json)",
    "Intra-layer relations are not drawn: {'presentation': 3, 'application': 5, 'domain': 16, 'persistence': 1}",
    "Layers come from package names (boundary, controller, entity, database): NotificationServiceAdapter and ExternalEmailGateway sit in the boundary package and therefore in Presentation, although they are an infrastructure adapter",
    "Web client (static/reservation.html, which posts to /reservations/create) and RestExceptionHandler have no code dependency on the other components and are not drawn",
    "Interfaces merged into their only implementation among the candidates: AssignmentStrategy into FirstAvailableAssignment, NotificationService into NotificationServiceAdapter, Observer into NotificationManager, ReservationState into ActiveState (the other four states were not examined as components)",
    "Dependencies were gathered by reading the code, not by a static analyser, so omissions are possible (reflexion divergence could not be computed)",
    "2 dependencies point against the layer order: Reservation (domain) -> NotificationManager (application); NotificationManager (application) -> NotificationServiceAdapter (presentation)"
  ],
